[
  {
    "ID": 1007440760,
    "key": "5d761fd9b5a65cd65d7c9aae052355f8a5f3b941c9786b0badbdb4178b3948ed",
    "original": "As you approach...",
    "translation": "当你接近时……",
    "stage": 1,
    "context": "this.m.Title = \"As you approach...\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440761,
    "key": "282d3093a6434fd8ee0a81c94c6a6371c0d4b435f77f513250397b906f0cd271",
    "original": "Fall back for now.",
    "translation": "暂且撤退。",
    "stage": 1,
    "context": "Text = \"Fall back for now.\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440762,
    "key": "0094192d0c88f370712c0ad7d30d2f2efea181603510eaf446529e060a0e0d21",
    "original": "Prepare the attack.",
    "translation": "准备攻击。",
    "stage": 1,
    "context": "Text = \"Prepare the attack.\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440763,
    "key": "d9777c516140eb7d684618b89b80d1d5a7c0abb242c21b6da8cd5968e62ab1ce",
    "original": "The barrows come into view like old scars upon the land, their stones stacked with care that speaks of reverence rather than haste. Frost clings to everything, and even the wind seems reluctant to pass through the place. Your men slow their pace, glancing from mound to mound, as though expecting something to rise at any moment.\n\nA voice answers their unease. It comes from among the stones, low and droning, repeating words worn thin by centuries of use. A solitary figure stands watch over the graves, his form stiff and rimed with ice, chanting without pause or inflection. With each verse, the ground trembles, and hands break through the soil, followed by helms, mail, and dead eyes that fix upon the living.\n\nThe risen Barrowkin move with purpose, drawn together by the chant, their presence pressing down on the spirit. No man feels the urge to shout or boast here. Only the need to brace, to endure. The chanter's voice binds them, steady and unyielding, as if this was always how the barrows were meant to answer intruders.\n\n%randombrother% whispers that these mounds must hold more than bones, that no people would guard empty graves for this long. You weigh the promise of buried wealth against the certainty that once blades are drawn, the chant will only grow louder, and the dead more numerous.",
    "translation": "古冢映入眼帘，如同大地上一道道陈旧的伤疤，石块堆叠得一丝不苟，透着敬意而非仓促。冰霜附着在每样东西上，连风都不愿经过此地。你的手下放慢了脚步，目光从一座丘扫向另一座丘，仿佛随时会有什么从地底起身。\n\n一个声音回应了他们的不安。它来自石堆之间，低沉而单调，重复着被世代传颂得磨蚀不清的词句。一个孤影看守着墓群，身形僵硬，覆满冰霜，不带停顿或起伏地吟唱着。每念一颂，大地便震颤，泥土中钻出一只只手，接着是头盔、锁甲，以及盯着生者的死寂双瞳。\n\n起身的墓穴族行动有序，被吟唱引力聚拢，他们的存在沉沉地压在魂灵之上。没人想在这里叫喊或夸口。唯有咬牙、忍耐的念头。吟唱者的声音捆缚着他们，沉着而不动摇，仿佛古冢本就该这般回应入侵者。\n\n%randombrother% 低声说，这些土丘里一定不止有骨骸，没有哪个族群会守着空墓这么久。你掂量着地下财宝的许诺，也清楚一旦刀剑出鞘，吟唱只会更加响亮，而死者会越来越多。",
    "context": "this[4] + \"The barrows come into view like old scars upon the land, their stones stacked with care that speaks of reverence rather than haste. Frost clings to everything, and even the wind seems reluctant to pass through the place. Your men slow their pace, glancing from mound to mound, as though expecting something to rise at any moment.\n\nA voice answers their unease. It comes from among the stones, low and droning, repeating words worn thin by centuries of use. A solitary figure stands watch over the graves, his form stiff and rimed with ice, chanting without pause or inflection. With each verse, the ground trembles, and hands break through the soil, followed by helms, mail, and dead eyes that fix upon the living.\n\nThe risen Barrowkin move with purpose, drawn together by the chant, their presence pressing down on the spirit. No man feels the urge to shout or boast here. Only the need to brace, to endure. The chanter's voice binds them, steady and unyielding, as if this was always how the barrows were meant to answer intruders.\n\n%randombrother% whispers that these mounds must hold more than bones, that no people would guard empty graves for this long. You weigh the promise of buried wealth against the certainty that once blades are drawn, the chant will only grow louder, and the dead more numerous.\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440764,
    "key": "ef96bb995978386e10ef2bc6847a3178cc1c6f1dc3a118d4c1c2be64092d004e",
    "original": "The barrows give way to stonework as you approach the crypt, its entrance cut deep into the earth and sealed with slabs etched in symbols worn nearly smooth. This was no common grave. The air around it is colder still, heavy with the weight of time and remembrance, and your men fall quiet as if instinct demands it.\n\nFrom within comes the chant, steady and unbroken, echoing through stone corridors meant to carry it, rising and falling in a cadence that feels practiced beyond memory. The voice sends a dreadful chill down your spine, gnawing at any courage you thought you might have had. Momentarily, the ground around the crypt stirs, and the dead answer, rising from their cold slumber.\n\nThen you feel it: a presence deeper within. This place was built for one who mattered, a forgotten hero whose name once carried weight enough to warrant stone walls and sealed doors. %randombrother% mutters that men are not laid in crypts like this unless they earned it in blood and battle. If the stories are even half true, the place will be full of of arms and treasure worth killing for. The question is, are they worth dying for?",
    "translation": "接近地窟时，古冢逐渐让位于石砌结构，入口深凿入地，以刻满符号的石板封堵，那些符号已被磨得近乎无痕。这不是普通的墓穴。周围的空气愈发寒冷，沉甸甸地压着时间与记忆的分量，你的手下安静下来，仿佛本能要求如此。\n\n吟唱从深处传来，沉稳而不间断，在特意为之的石廊中回荡，起伏的节奏仿佛演练了超越记忆的岁月。那声音令一股可怕的寒意窜上你的脊背，蚕食着你自以为还有的那点勇气。顷刻间，地窟周围的土地翻动，死者回应，从冰冷的沉眠中起身。\n\n然后你感觉到了：更深处还有一个存在。这个地方是为某位重要之人而建，一个被遗忘的英雄，其名曾经分量十足，足以配得上石墙与封门。%randombrother% 咕哝说，人们不会把平凡之辈葬在这种地窟里，除非他们以血与战斗赢得了这份礼遇。即使传说只有一半是真的，这里也会满是值得为之厮杀的兵刃与财宝。问题在于，它们是否值得为之去死？",
    "context": "this[4] + \"The barrows give way to stonework as you approach the crypt, its entrance cut deep into the earth and sealed with slabs etched in symbols worn nearly smooth. This was no common grave. The air around it is colder still, heavy with the weight of time and remembrance, and your men fall quiet as if instinct demands it.\n\nFrom within comes the chant, steady and unbroken, echoing through stone corridors meant to carry it, rising and falling in a cadence that feels practiced beyond memory. The voice sends a dreadful chill down your spine, gnawing at any courage you thought you might have had. Momentarily, the ground around the crypt stirs, and the dead answer, rising from their cold slumber.\n\nThen you feel it: a presence deeper within. This place was built for one who mattered, a forgotten hero whose name once carried weight enough to warrant stone walls and sealed doors. %randombrother% mutters that men are not laid in crypts like this unless they earned it in blood and battle. If the stories are even half true, the place will be full of of arms and treasure worth killing for. The question is, are they worth dying for?\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440765,
    "key": "a1272e234eb6e239cb491330b35a44ad774acd750ca313bc65615f962549ff09",
    "original": "The crypt rises from the frost like a clenched fist of stone, its entrance marked by carvings of warriors long since stripped of name and meaning. Snow lies undisturbed before it, but the stillness feels forced, held in place by something watching from within. Your breath fogs as the cold deepens, seeping through mail and fur alike.\n\nA chant echoes from the dark beyond the doorway, its rhythm measured and patient, as if time itself bends around it. The voice carries through soil and stone as the earth answers. Barrowkin rise, clad in armor that speaks of deliberate honor rather than mass burial.\n\nSomewhere behind those walls, you sense a heavier tread waiting. This crypt was raised to hold a hero, a figure venerated enough to be sealed away with weapons and relics meant to follow them into whatever came after. The dead outside do not wander. They hold ground, as though guarding the moment yet to come.\n\n%randombrother% says this place reeks of old glory and old mistakes, and that crypts like these are never empty-handed. You know he's thinking of famed steel and grave-goods untouched by living hands, but first you'll have to silence the chant that keeps raising the dead.",
    "translation": "地窟自冻土中耸起，像一只握紧的石头拳头，入口处刻着战士的雕纹，那些战士的名字与意义早已磨灭。入口前的雪未被扰动，但这份静止却透着被迫之感，仿佛被内部某个注视的东西压制着。寒意加深，你的呼吸凝成白雾，渗过锁甲与皮毛。\n\n吟唱从门扉后的黑暗中传来，节奏沉稳而耐心，仿佛时间本身都为之弯曲。那声音穿透土壤与岩石，大地回应。墓穴族们起身，身披的盔甲透露出刻意为之的荣耀，而非乱葬的随意。\n\n在那几堵石墙后的某处，你察觉到更沉重的脚步在等待。这座地窟是为一位英雄建造的，一位深受尊崇的人物，因此被随葬的兵刃与圣物一同封存，伴他通往来世。外面的死者并不游荡。他们坚守阵地，仿佛在守护着即将到来的那一刻。\n\n%randombrother% 说，这地方散发着旧日荣耀与旧日错误的气味，这样的地窟从来不会空手而归。你知道他正想着那些名扬四海的钢剑和未曾被活人触碰过的墓中财物，但首先你得让那不断唤醒死者的吟唱沉默下来。",
    "context": "this[4] + \"The crypt rises from the frost like a clenched fist of stone, its entrance marked by carvings of warriors long since stripped of name and meaning. Snow lies undisturbed before it, but the stillness feels forced, held in place by something watching from within. Your breath fogs as the cold deepens, seeping through mail and fur alike.\n\nA chant echoes from the dark beyond the doorway, its rhythm measured and patient, as if time itself bends around it. The voice carries through soil and stone as the earth answers. Barrowkin rise, clad in armor that speaks of deliberate honor rather than mass burial.\n\nSomewhere behind those walls, you sense a heavier tread waiting. This crypt was raised to hold a hero, a figure venerated enough to be sealed away with weapons and relics meant to follow them into whatever came after. The dead outside do not wander. They hold ground, as though guarding the moment yet to come.\n\n%randombrother% says this place reeks of old glory and old mistakes, and that crypts like these are never empty-handed. You know he's thinking of famed steel and grave-goods untouched by living hands, but first you'll have to silence the chant that keeps raising the dead.\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440766,
    "key": "1963eddf3f23a9f89dcab4f905829911ecd535878c6b05055e4304681e75eda3",
    "original": "The fane is carved into the mountain itself, its stone face worked into pillars and lintels that once marked a hall of gathering. Wind howls through the entrance, carrying with it a chill that feels older than the snow beneath your boots. This place was not built to hide the dead, but to house them in state.\n\nWithin, a chant echoes from vaulted stone, deep and resonant, as though the mountain answers it in kind. A lone chanter stands at the threshold, his voice rising and falling in a cadence that feels ceremonial rather than watchful. At his call, the dead emerge, stepping forth from shadowed halls and sealed chambers.\n\nThese Barrowkin bear the marks of rank and lineage. Their armor is decorated, their weapons wrought with care, and they move with the certainty of those who were once followed into battle. The chant binds them together while pressing down on your men like the weight of an unseen crowd, smothering any spark of bravado before it can take hold.\n\n%randombrother% speaks low, naming this place a hall of ancestors, the kind raised for kings, champions, and those buried with their kin and their warbands alike. There will be riches here beyond counting, he says, but they were never meant for the living. To take them, you will have to break the rite that keeps the dead enthroned and face whatever champions wait deep within.",
    "translation": "这座圣殿凿刻于山体之中，岩石立面被雕成立柱与楣梁，曾是一座集会大厅的入口。寒风呼啸着灌入，携带着一股比脚下积雪更为古老的寒意。此处并非为藏匿死者而建，而是为了以庄严之姿安置他们。\n\n殿内，拱形石顶下回荡着吟唱，低沉而浑厚，仿佛山岳本身在与之应和。一名孤独的吟唱者立于门廊，他的声音起伏有致，节奏更像仪式而非警戒。随着他的呼唤，死者现身，从幽暗的厅堂与封闭的墓室中走出。\n\n这些墓穴族带有阶级与血统的印记。他们的甲胄饰有纹样，武器精心锻造，行动间透着昔日追随者冲锋陷阵的笃定。吟唱将他们凝聚在一起，同时如同一片无形的人群沉重地压在你的手下身上，任何一丝虚张声势的火花在燃起之前便被扼杀。\n\n%randombrother% 低声说，此处名为先祖之殿，是为国王、勇士以及与其亲族和战团合葬者所建。他说，这里的财宝不可胜数，却从未属于活人。若想取走，你必须打破令死者稳坐王座的仪式，并直面深处等待着的那些勇士。",
    "context": "this[4] + \"The fane is carved into the mountain itself, its stone face worked into pillars and lintels that once marked a hall of gathering. Wind howls through the entrance, carrying with it a chill that feels older than the snow beneath your boots. This place was not built to hide the dead, but to house them in state.\n\nWithin, a chant echoes from vaulted stone, deep and resonant, as though the mountain answers it in kind. A lone chanter stands at the threshold, his voice rising and falling in a cadence that feels ceremonial rather than watchful. At his call, the dead emerge, stepping forth from shadowed halls and sealed chambers.\n\nThese Barrowkin bear the marks of rank and lineage. Their armor is decorated, their weapons wrought with care, and they move with the certainty of those who were once followed into battle. The chant binds them together while pressing down on your men like the weight of an unseen crowd, smothering any spark of bravado before it can take hold.\n\n%randombrother% speaks low, naming this place a hall of ancestors, the kind raised for kings, champions, and those buried with their kin and their warbands alike. There will be riches here beyond counting, he says, but they were never meant for the living. To take them, you will have to break the rite that keeps the dead enthroned and face whatever champions wait deep within.\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440767,
    "key": "11ab670321b432a4b69eac77e64254f227fc9221468b057098a3b631956fc292",
    "original": "The land rises into low, rounded mounds of stone and frozen earth, each marked by crude standing slabs worn smooth by wind and time. The air here is unnaturally still, the cold sharper than it should be, and your men grow quiet without being told. Whatever was buried in these barrows was meant to stay undisturbed.\n\nThen you hear it. A chant, slow and measured, carried across the stones like a funeral dirge without end. At the center of the mounds stands a lone figure, unmoving, his voice grinding on as if he has never known fatigue. As the chant continues, the earth itself begins to answer, barrow after barrow cracking open as pale shapes claw their way free.\n\nWeapons are drawn as the dead rise, some little more than frozen thralls, others clad in ancient mail that still bears the marks of careful burial. Their voices rasp as they move, not quite speech, not quite breath, and the sound sets teeth on edge. The chanting does not falter, nor does the chanter acknowledge your presence.\n\n%randombrother% mutters that these graves were stocked with offerings. Coin, arms, perhaps relics meant to honor the dead, and that such places are rarely poor. You know he's right, but as the chant presses down on your thoughts and the dead gather in number, it's clear that any riches here will be paid for in blood.",
    "translation": "大地隆起成低矮浑圆的土丘，由碎石与冻土堆成，每座丘上都立着粗粝的石板，被风与岁月磨得光滑。这里的空气静得诡异，寒意比别处更刺骨，你的手下不待吩咐便纷纷沉默下来。无论这些古冢里埋着什么，本不该被打扰。\n\n然后你听到了。一段吟唱，缓慢而沉稳，越过石块传来，仿佛永无止境的挽歌。在丘群中央立着一个孤独的身影，纹丝不动，他的声音像砂石碾磨，似乎从不曾感到疲倦。随着吟唱继续，大地开始回应，一座座古冢裂开，惨白的身影破土而出。\n\n死者起身时，武器出鞘——有些不过是冻僵的奴仆，另一些则穿着古代锁子甲，甲上仍留着精心入葬的痕迹。他们移动时喉咙发出嘶哑的声音，不像说话，也不像呼吸，那声响让人牙根发酸。吟唱不曾中断，吟唱者也不曾理会你们的存在。\n\n%randombrother% 嘀咕着，这些墓穴里应该随葬了供品——钱币、武器，或许是用来敬奉死者的圣物，这样的地方很少穷困。你知道他说得对，但随着吟唱压迫着你的思绪，死者的数量越聚越多，有一点很清楚：这里的任何财富，都得用血来换。",
    "context": "this[4] + \"The land rises into low, rounded mounds of stone and frozen earth, each marked by crude standing slabs worn smooth by wind and time. The air here is unnaturally still, the cold sharper than it should be, and your men grow quiet without being told. Whatever was buried in these barrows was meant to stay undisturbed.\n\nThen you hear it. A chant, slow and measured, carried across the stones like a funeral dirge without end. At the center of the mounds stands a lone figure, unmoving, his voice grinding on as if he has never known fatigue. As the chant continues, the earth itself begins to answer, barrow after barrow cracking open as pale shapes claw their way free.\n\nWeapons are drawn as the dead rise, some little more than frozen thralls, others clad in ancient mail that still bears the marks of careful burial. Their voices rasp as they move, not quite speech, not quite breath, and the sound sets teeth on edge. The chanting does not falter, nor does the chanter acknowledge your presence.\n\n%randombrother% mutters that these graves were stocked with offerings. Coin, arms, perhaps relics meant to honor the dead, and that such places are rarely poor. You know he's right, but as the chant presses down on your thoughts and the dead gather in number, it's clear that any riches here will be paid for in blood.\""
  },
  {
    "ID": 1007440768,
    "key": "86d8d04b8a4ddcbe5dfc899f2253ad4a9d43c84aa25547637c6aefe44743ac65",
    "original": "The mountain's face has been shaped into something that resembles a hall rather than a tomb, its entrance wide and deliberate. Stone pillars rise like frozen sentinels, their carvings dulled by centuries of wind and ice. This is no ordinary burial hall, it is a place built to endure the grinding of time.\n\nA chant fills the fane, echoing from deep within, layered and heavy, as though repeated by voices long since stilled. The chanter stands unmoving, his vigil uninterrupted by your approach, and with every measured verse more of the dead take their places. They do not rise in disorder; they assemble.\n\nYou feel eyes upon you from the dark beyond the pillars. Somewhere in the depths lie those for whom this hall was raised. Kings, heroes of ages past, buried with their families, their guards, and the relics of their rule. The dead outside hold their ground, as if awaiting the moment their betters are called to rise.\n\n%randombrother% mutters that fanes like this are spoken of in old tales, where clans gathered to honor their rulers even after death. If the stories hold true, then famed arms and ancient wealth lie within, but so do the dead who were trusted to wield them forever.",
    "translation": "山体被雕琢成一座更像大殿而非坟墓的形态，入口宽阔而精心。石柱如冰封的哨兵般耸立，其雕刻历经数个世纪的风雪与寒冰而变得暗淡。这不是一座普通的墓葬大殿，而是一个为抵御时间侵蚀而建的地方。\n\n吟唱充满了整座圣殿，从深处回荡而来，层层叠叠，沉重浑厚，仿佛由早已沉寂的声音反复吟诵。吟唱者纹丝不动，你们的到来并未打断他的守望，每念一颂，便有更多的死者各就各位。他们并非混乱地起身，而是在列阵。\n\n你感到有目光从石柱后的黑暗中注视着你。深处的某处，躺着这座大殿为之而建的那些人——往昔的国王、英雄，与他们的家族、护卫以及统治的圣物一同埋葬。外面的死者坚守阵地，仿佛在等待他们的尊主被唤醒的时刻。\n\n%randombrother%咕哝说，这样的圣殿在老故事里曾被提及，部族死后仍聚集在此以敬奉他们的统治者。若传说属实，那么知名的兵器与古老的财富就在其中，但同时还有那些被托付永远挥舞它们的死者。",
    "context": "this[4] + \"The mountain's face has been shaped into something that resembles a hall rather than a tomb, its entrance wide and deliberate. Stone pillars rise like frozen sentinels, their carvings dulled by centuries of wind and ice. This is no ordinary burial hall, it is a place built to endure the grinding of time.\n\nA chant fills the fane, echoing from deep within, layered and heavy, as though repeated by voices long since stilled. The chanter stands unmoving, his vigil uninterrupted by your approach, and with every measured verse more of the dead take their places. They do not rise in disorder; they assemble.\n\nYou feel eyes upon you from the dark beyond the pillars. Somewhere in the depths lie those for whom this hall was raised. Kings, heroes of ages past, buried with their families, their guards, and the relics of their rule. The dead outside hold their ground, as if awaiting the moment their betters are called to rise.\n\n%randombrother% mutters that fanes like this are spoken of in old tales, where clans gathered to honor their rulers even after death. If the stories hold true, then famed arms and ancient wealth lie within, but so do the dead who were trusted to wield them forever.\""
  }
]
